; Item sprites: the doorway arch (16x24) and 14 sprites of 16x16 pixels
;
; Plain (unpacked) sprite graphics, 16 pixels wide: 2 bytes per pixel row, no mask (the outline comes from the table
; built at $FF00 by #R$6000). They are not copied to the sprite sheet: the frame lists at #R$8B07 point here and the
; sprite drawer reads them directly (popping 2 bytes per row, see #R$98F7). A frame is selected by the item handlers
; from #R$A600 on; frames are listed with the item they belong to.
; .
; +$0000 SpriteArch: doorway arch, 24 rows (48 bytes), the passage between rooms 10 and 19
; +$0030 SpriteCheckpoint0: checkpoint (cross in a ring), not yet touched
; +$0050 SpriteCheckpoint1: checkpoint, active
; +$0070 SpriteBell0: bell at rest (Tower of the Bell)
; +$0090 SpriteBell1: bell swinging
; +$00B0 SpriteLever0: lever, not pulled
; +$00D0 SpriteLever1: lever, pulled
; +$00F0 SpriteWheel0: the wheel of faith at rest
; +$0110 SpriteWheel1: the wheel of faith turned (ornate frame)
; +$0130 SpriteChalice: the chalice in Satan's room
; +$0150 SpriteHeart0, +$0170 SpriteHeart1: heart (extra life), two frames (beating)
; +$0190 SpriteCross: cross, drawn in six colours by the frame lists
; +$01B0 SpritePlus: plus-shaped cross, the other look of the crosses: the frame lists #R$8B07 repeat the cross in six colours as SpriteCross and as SpritePlus, and #R$A777/#R$A782 pick one depending on the wheel of faith (#R$851E)
; +$01D0 SpriteScroll: parchment; drawn red for the scroll that ends the game
@label=SpriteArch
